# Step 28, its third pull request's first part: custom commands, headless
# mode's side, broken one at a time, with the tests that must fail.

[break] headless-does-not-say-whose-command-it-sends
rule: Headless mode says on standard error which command it sends, whose it is and its file, before it runs.
os: linux
file: crates/cineris-cli/src/headless.rs
in: in_core
find: front.say(&said);
replace: let _ = &said;
caught-by:
    cineris-cli::system signals::sys_ctrl_c_stops_a_running_extension_command
